{"name":"Still Waters Run Deep","hex":"#4a5d5f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"still waters run deep","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proverb","definitions":["A person with a calm appearance has, or may have, considerable inner emotion, character, or intellect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still_waters_run_deep"}],"entries":[{"title":"Still waters run deep","blocks":[{"text":"\"Still waters run deep\" is a proverb of Latin origin now commonly taken to mean that a placid exterior hides a passionate or subtle nature. Formerly it also carried the warning that silent people are dangerous, as in Suffolk's comment on a fellow lord in William Shakespeare's play Henry VI part 2:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_waters_run_deep"},{"title":"Still Waters Run Deep (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Still Waters Run Deep is the ninth studio album by the American vocal group Four Tops."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/Four-tops-still-waters-run-deep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_Waters_Run_Deep_(album)"},{"title":"Deva Mahal","blocks":[{"text":"Deva Salote Mahal is a soul and R&B singer. Mahal is the daughter of American blues musician Taj Mahal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Deva_Mahal_3.jpg/330px-Deva_Mahal_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deva_Mahal"},{"title":"Still","blocks":[{"text":"A still is an apparatus used to distill liquid mixtures by heating to selectively boil and then cooling to condense the vapor. A still uses the same concepts as a basic distillation apparatus, but on a much larger scale. Stills have been used to produce perfume and medicine, water for injection (WFI) for pharmaceutical use, generally to separate and purify different chemicals, and to produce distilled beverages containing ethanol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg/330px-Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Grandville_torrent.jpg/330px-Grandville_torrent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Grandville_torrent.jpg/330px-Grandville_torrent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"J. J. Grandville's interpretation of La Fontaine's fable from the 1855 edition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrandville_torrent.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/1280px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A still at Mackmyra Whisky Distillery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Coffey_Still.JPG/500px-Coffey_Still.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Coffey_Still.JPG/1280px-Coffey_Still.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"ht